  "summary": "New preprints pair 5xFAD snRNA-seq, harmonized mouse transcriptomes and large cortical miRNA data to resolve cell-type mechanisms in Alzheimer's disease.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is cell-type-resolved omics applied to Alzheimer's disease and its models. In 5xFAD mouse brain, snRNA-seq identifies VIP interneurons as most disrupted in synapse programs and preferentially rescued by rolipram, implicating a Pde7b/CREB1 cAMP axis. A harmonized set of 1,863 mouse cortex and hippocampus samples, including AD models, enables uniform cross-study comparison. A separate study links early lysosomal biogenesis (MiT/TFE) to disease-associated microglia reprogramming across murine injury, amyloidosis and human AD. In humans, a meta-analysis of 1,738 postmortem cortices connects miRNAs, notably miR-132-3p, to tau pathology and cell-type programs. Developmental regulatory maps from 231 prefrontal cortices and VEGABrain extend this toward developmental context. The preeclampsia miRNA-mRNA study is peripheral to this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
